ORD, what is man, that You regard him, the son of man that You think of him?","verse":3},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"Part Your heavens, O LORD, and come down; touch the mountains, that they may smoke.","verse":5},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"Blessed are the people of whom this is so; blessed are the people whose God is the LORD.","verse":15}],"id":"Lord","label":"LORD","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","scope":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","senseReview":"Only literal uppercase LORD is admitted globally. Source Lord article explicitly covers God as Lord; lowercase human lord and sentence-title Lord are not inferred from this rule.","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord","term":"LORD"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Lord","sourceTitle":"Lord"}],"format":"bsb-study-chapter-v2","notes":[{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.138.1-145.21","r":"Ps.138.1-145.21","rawR":"Ps.138.1-145.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.138.1-145.21","value":"Ps.138.1-145.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 138–145"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," In this final collection of psalms of David, praise and wisdom psalms (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.138.1-139.24","r":"Ps.138.1-139.24","rawR":"Ps.138.1-139.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.138.1-139.24","value":"Ps.138.1-139.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 138–139"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.145.1-21","r":"Ps.145.1-21","rawR":"Ps.145.1-21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.145.1-21","value":"Ps.145.1-21"}],"t":"ref","v":"145"},") form a frame around five poems of lament (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.140.1-144.15","r":"Ps.140.1-144.15","rawR":"Ps.140.1-144.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.140.1-144.15","value":"Ps.140.1-144.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 140–144"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.138.1-145.21","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":145,"endVerse":21,"startChapter":138,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.138.1-145.21","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[138,139,140,141,142,143,144,145],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"635758a56903b7b4813131c900a660965334f93d93f552c627645cb63ca925dc","sourceItemName":"Ps.138.1-145.21","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7386,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.138.1-145.21","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.138.1-145.21","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.144.1-15","r":"Ps.144.1-15","rawR":"Ps.144.1-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.144.1-15","value":"Ps.144.1-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 144"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," This lament begins with an exclamation of love for the Lord. The community then reflects on the transitory nature of life (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.144.3-4","r":"Ps.144.3-4","rawR":"Ps.144.3-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.144.3-4","value":"Ps.144.3-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"144:3-4"},"). The psalmist prays for divine intervention and anticipates victory (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.144.5-11","r":"Ps.144.5-11","rawR":"Ps.144.5-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.144.5-11","value":"Ps.144.5-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"144:5-11"},"). A new song (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.144.9-10","r":"Ps.144.9-10","rawR":"Ps.144.9-10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.144.9-10","value":"Ps.144.9-10"}],"t":"ref","v":"144:9-10"},") and a prayer for rescue (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.144.11","r":"Ps.144.11","rawR":"Ps.144.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.144.11","value":"Ps.144.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"144:11"},") open up the theme of the Lord’s blessing through his provisions and protection (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.144.12-15","r":"Ps.144.12-15","rawR":"Ps.144.12-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.144.12-15","value":"Ps.144.12-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"144:12-15"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.144.1-15","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":144,"endVerse":15,"startChapter":144,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.144.1-15","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[144],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"b86b97f03429248b0fcbb1e29bd3af95380da1d4a1f7dc6e99e43573aa173738","sourceItemName":"Ps.144.1-15","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7435,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.144.1-15","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.144.1-15","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.144.1-2","r":"Ps.144.1-2","rawR":"Ps.144.1-2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.144.1-2","value":"Ps.144.1-2"}],"t":"ref","v":"144:1-2"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The psalmist’s descriptive names for the Lord reveal his deep love for him."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.144.1-2","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":144,"endVerse":2,"startChapter":144,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.144.1-2","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[144],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"68cc26ed2c436e414216c1a01857026608310ff1a54a8f77e0cb77b641387090","sourceItemName":"Ps.144.1-2","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7436,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.144.1-2","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.144.1-2","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.144.3-4","r":"Ps.144.3-4","rawR":"Ps.144.3-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.144.3-4","value":"Ps.144.3-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"144:3-4"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["what are human beings?"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," The same question in ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.8.4-6","r":"Ps.8.4-6","rawR":"Ps.8.4-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.8.4-6","value":"Ps.8.4-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:4-6"}," elicits the answer that humans are mere mortals but are also glorious rulers. The psalmist depicts humans as having a transitory, empty existence (see ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.90.3","r":"Ps.90.3","rawR":"Ps.90.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.90.3","value":"Ps.90.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"90:3"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.90.7-10","r":"Ps.90.7-10","rawR":"Ps.90.7-10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.90.7-10","value":"Ps.90.7-10"}],"t":"ref","v":"7-10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.102.11","r":"Ps.102.11","rawR":"Ps.102.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.102.11","value":"Ps.102.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"102:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.109.23","r":"Ps.109.23","rawR":"Ps.109.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.109.23","value":"Ps.109.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"109:23"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.146.4","r":"Ps.146.4","rawR":"Ps.146.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.146.4","value":"Ps.146.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"146:4"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.144.3-4","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":144,"endVerse":4,"startChapter":144,"startVerse":3}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.144.3-4","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[144],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"08f0f2074ec7851c19cd8079805f4b670169f76611fc86dead57707b618090cb","sourceItemName":"Ps.144.3-4","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7437,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.144.3-4","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.144.3-4","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.144.5-8","r":"Ps.144.5-8","rawR":"Ps.144.5-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.144.5-8","value":"Ps.144.5-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"144:5-8"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The psalmist prays for God’s intervention against his ",{"c":["enemies"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," (cp. ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.18.7-19","r":"Ps.18.7-19","rawR":"Ps.18.7-19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.18.7-19","value":"Ps.18.7-19"}],"t":"ref","v":"18:7-19"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.144.5-8","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":144,"endVerse":8,"startChapter":144,"startVerse":5}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.144.5-8","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[144],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"608ff732474612cab56526a74bcf91cfe5ec256a16ba1cdadc9d77964f3ac294","sourceItemName":"Ps.144.5-8","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7438,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.144.5-8","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.144.5-8","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.144.12-15","r":"Ps.144.12-15","rawR":"Ps.144.12-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.144.12-15","value":"Ps.144.12-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"144:12-15"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," This prayer for the Lord’s blessing brings the laments of ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.140.1-144.15","r":"Ps.140.1-144.15","rawR":"Ps.140.1-144.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.140.1-144.15","value":"Ps.140.1-144.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 140–144"}," to a close. It offers a vision of God’s provision and protection (see ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.127.1-5","r":"Ps.127.1-5","rawR":"Ps.127.1-5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.127.1-5","value":"Ps.127.1-5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 127"},"), not only for the psalmist, but for his descendants and those of all the godly."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.144.12-15","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":144,"endVerse":15,"startChapter":144,"startVerse":12}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.144.12-15","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[144],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"cee5d038d76a9480bf97505a4b8f9e280dfd3f53311305f9c3e35f878496dfba","sourceItemName":"Ps.144.12-15","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7439,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.144.12-15","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.144.12-15","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.144.12","r":"Ps.144.12","rawR":"Ps.144.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.144.12","value":"Ps.144.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"144:12"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The psalmist compares ",{"c":["sons"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," and ",{"c":["daughters"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," to plants and pillars, which are images of strength and beauty."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.144.12","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":144,"endVerse":12,"startChapter":144,"startVerse":12}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.144.12","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[144],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"1b56f5ca17ef4a15809840c12d1fd6b61aa39d31acabcb594464afd7340056d7","sourceItemName":"Ps.144.12","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7440,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.144.12","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.144.12","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.144.13-14","r":"Ps.144.13-14","rawR":"Ps.144.13-14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.144.13-14","value":"Ps.144.13-14"}],"t":"ref","v":"144:13-14"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["no enemy . . . no cries of alarm:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," These images depict peace and security."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.144.13-14","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":144,"endVerse":14,"startChapter":144,"startVerse":13}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.144.13-14","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[144],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"d9ef60f3ab7a862c5abe9111a8e08c613999e313adbdeac6b7071a392e9ce